{"time": 1793826453.7584107, "event": "prepared", "backend": "robot", "policy": "astra", "model": "gpt-6.1-terra", "pause_world": false, "walk": false, "follow": true, "task_name": "follow_balloon", "task": "A red balloon is in front of the robot (in simulation, a red sphere): a person may hold\nit, move it to new places, or leave it on a stand or on the floor, for the robot to take it. You set\nthe robot's intent; a local 20 Hz controller carries it out immediately, so you never time\na grab or a release yourself:\n- catch: follow the balloon, close the arms around it as soon as it is still and within\n  reach, hold it while it stays in the hands, let go the moment the person pulls it out,\n  then follow it and grab it again.\n- follow: follow the balloon at a comfortable distance without grabbing it.\n- release: let go now and keep following without grabbing until catch is chosen again.\n- hold: keep the intent that is in force.\ncontroller.tracker is the local estimate when these images were taken: mode (follow or\nhold), intent (in force), whether the balloon is visible and still, and its position x_m\n(forward) and y_m (left) of the pelvis. Choose catch as soon as any part of the red\nballoon is visible in the images: held by a person, on a stand, lying on the floor, low,\nfar away, or at the edge of the image, whether it is moving or still (the controller follows it while\nit moves and closes the arms only once it has stopped within reach), unless something makes\ngrabbing it unsafe; once catch is in force, answer hold. Choose follow or release only if\ngrabbing would be wrong, stop if anything is unsafe, and hold when unsure.", "max_decisions": 200, "max_decision_age": 2}
